{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/822738-question-on-the-wyld","id":822738,"title":"Question on the wyld","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-03T14:10:53-08:00","id":822738,"title":"Question on the wyld","content":"Are there any books where the wyld is serious threat? Most of the material in werewolf has bad guys connected to the wyrm/weaver with a side mention about the weakening of the wyld, or have the werewolves work with a wyld aligned entity(like fae or marauders). It just seems a little strange to me as the wyld seems like it has by far the Most potential for becoming the bad guy(wyld aligned entity that was helping a pack most of the story suddenly turns on them causing them to fail, sudden manifestation of a wyld spirit destroying a cairn, etc.)<br /> <br /> I also find the &quot;Wyld is weakening&quot; alittle hard to believe as chaotic things in nature(example: stars) have a tendency of burning evenly for long periods of time before going into dormancy. In said dormancy, it waits for a set of circumstances to be fulfilled before reacting violently with more force and power than it has held its entire life(Link to example: stars nearing the end of their lives will go into a regresion cycle where the red giant will start outputting far less heat and begin shrinking into itself. As heat and pressure builds in its core a cascading fussion reaction will occur causing the star to eat all of it's fuel at once and will explode outward with immeasurable force in a process called a &quot;Super Nova&quot;). Afterward said chaos will lose energy and a newly created one will take its place(the material created by stars going supernova spreads across space and re collects to form entire solar systems).<br /> <br /> So isn't it possible that the Wyld is just in its dormancy cycle and is waiting for the right conditions before it unleashes itself upon the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T17:42:47-08:00","id":822913,"title":"","content":"Yes. The Book of the Wyld implies that it might be going in for payback, as close as something like the Wyld could be said to, and introduces Thresholds, where the Wyld has bled through from its effective exile into the Umbra and into the physical world with... troubling results. In caerns, these are known as abcesses, and not even Black Furies tolerate them. In fact, the Furies are the foremost keepers of the rite to cut thresholds off and send them back into the spirit world. Gorgons are also presented as strange and possibly not always on the side of Gaia; Possessed expands upon this, since gorgons also use Autonomy rather than being balanced and in-harmony like kami, and also share a few bizarre and unnatural capacities with fomori.<br /> <br /> As for wonders farther off into the universe, consider that the Wyld requires spirit and matter to be as one to really do its thing, rather than concerning yourself with real-world cosmology. That wonders exist among the stars gives its brand of potential and chaos some hope, but the world is broken, and so it isn't what it could be... unless it applies itself with such brute force that it might well cause another, even worse problem in retaliating against the other two Supernals of the Triat. Book of the Wyld directly mentions a number of horror and disaster movies as example inspiration; Even a zombie apocalypse isn't out of the question, because hey, we're talking about the sum of all possibilities known and unknown here.<br /> <br /> Edit: Various beings from other games are, at best, &quot;Wyld-aligned&quot; in the vaguest, loosest possible use of the term. Changelings are going to get Unleashing in C20, though, so they might have a closer &quot;affinity&quot;, in that they can produce a horrifyingly unpredictable effect of terrible potency which they cannot fully control. And that's what the Wyld can be, and often likely is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 02-03-2016, 08:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T23:16:04-08:00","id":823101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/822738-question-on-the-wyld?p=822913#post822913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: Various beings from other games are, at best, &quot;Wyld-aligned&quot; in the vaguest, loosest possible use of the term. Changelings are going to get Unleashing in C20, though, so they might have a closer &quot;affinity&quot;, in that they can produce a horrifyingly unpredictable effect of terrible potency which they cannot fully control. And that's what the Wyld can be, and often likely is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some of the Dark Age Fey seem ideal for portraying rampant Wyld faerie types, compared to their tame modern cousins.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T23:52:04-08:00","id":823120,"title":"","content":"If you really want to get crazy run nonsense that was &quot;the happening&quot;......","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T09:08:27-08:00","id":823417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/822738-question-on-the-wyld?p=822913#post822913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for wonders farther off into the universe, consider that the Wyld requires spirit and matter to be as one to really do its thing, rather than concerning yourself with real-world cosmology. That wonders exist among the stars gives its brand of potential and chaos some hope, but the world is broken, and so it isn't what it could be... unless it applies itself with such brute force that it might well cause another, even worse problem in retaliating against the other two Supernals of the Triat. Book of the Wyld directly mentions a number of horror and disaster movies as example inspiration; Even a zombie apocalypse isn't out of the question, because hey, we're talking about the sum of all possibilities known and unknown here.</div> </div> </div> </div>The world is not necessarily broken as in a low cycle, a friend of mine made a convincing case, its very likely that the triat is never so much in &quot;Balance&quot; as it exists in cycles(like how dark ages fae look at the seasons).<br /> <br /> Look at the Mokole's age of dragon kings, the mokole gained intelligence during a time without technology and survival was the order of the day(wyld rule), with their new found intelligence and ability to communicate through menesis they created their own society(weaver overtaking wyld), and created an era of peace(weaver rule). After the thousands of years that it existed their society likely never changed(weaver grows to powerful), a line of naturally accuring events began to break down their society(a combination of a meteor and several volcanic eruptions blocking out the sun,I.E. the wyrm growing restless), and the distruction left in its wake destroys said society(wyrm rule, though the mokole at the time probably thought it was the death of gaia.). During the time of destruction survival is once again the order of the day(wyrm is quickly overtaken by the wyld), and the the animals tha are left change in order to survive(the evolution of mamals and birds, wyld rule).<br /> <br /> Afterwards the triat is back where it started, only with a Larger variety of changing breeds than before and the introduction of humans, a naturally evolved species using its intelligence to build a new society.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T18:54:35-08:00","id":823929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/822738-question-on-the-wyld?p=823417#post823417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The world is not necessarily broken as in a low cycle, a friend of mine made a convincing case, its very likely that the triat is never so much in &quot;Balance&quot; as it exists in cycles(like how dark ages fae look at the seasons).<br /> <br /> Look at the Mokole's age of dragon kings, the mokole gained intelligence during a time without technology and survival was the order of the day(wyld rule), with their new found intelligence and ability to communicate through menesis they created their own society(weaver overtaking wyld), and created an era of peace(weaver rule). After the thousands of years that it existed their society likely never changed(weaver grows to powerful), a line of naturally accuring events began to break down their society(a combination of a meteor and several volcanic eruptions blocking out the sun,I.E. the wyrm growing restless), and the distruction left in its wake destroys said society(wyrm rule, though the mokole at the time probably thought it was the death of gaia.). During the time of destruction survival is once again the order of the day(wyrm is quickly overtaken by the wyld), and the the animals tha are left change in order to survive(the evolution of mamals and birds, wyld rule).<br /> <br /> Afterwards the triat is back where it started, only with a Larger variety of changing breeds than before and the introduction of humans, a naturally evolved species using its intelligence to build a new society.....</div> </div> </div> </div>Renewal is great but not something that you can expect. Also, having the Wyld as ascendant doesn't necessarily entail a lack of technology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T00:10:01-08:00","id":824069,"title":"","content":"It's one of the things that gets very muddled with statments that any of the splats &quot;Serve&quot; the Wyld. The Wyld is impersonal random change for the sake of change. It's not particularly friendly and it does not have servants like the Weaver or the Wyrm. The things it has are essentially loci of madness and spontaneous change. I'm not even sure it has any agenda or goals, because it just is.<br /> <br /> I am assuming this came from the problem that some of the writers saw Weaver and Wyrm as &quot;bad&quot; and conculuded the Wyld must be good. The truth is that none of the triat gives a damn about good or bad (ok, a part of the Wyrm wants to drag the world down screaming). The only real difference is that the Weaver and the Wyrm are more organised about pursuing their core principles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T09:15:37-08:00","id":824366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/822738-question-on-the-wyld?p=823929#post823929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Renewal is great but not something that you can expect. Also, having the Wyld as ascendant doesn't necessarily entail a lack of technology.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Right, And I didn't mean to imply that it did. I just meant that technology hadn't been invented yet in the time before dinosaurs.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/822738-question-on-the-wyld?p=824069#post824069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's one of the things that gets very muddled with statments that any of the splats &quot;Serve&quot; the Wyld. The Wyld is impersonal random change for the sake of change. It's not particularly friendly and it does not have servants like the Weaver or the Wyrm. The things it has are essentially loci of madness and spontaneous change. I'm not even sure it has any agenda or goals, because it just is.<br /> <br /> I am assuming this came from the problem that some of the writers saw Weaver and Wyrm as &quot;bad&quot; and conculuded the Wyld must be good. The truth is that none of the triat gives a damn about good or bad (ok, a part of the Wyrm wants to drag the world down screaming). The only real difference is that the Weaver and the Wyrm are more organised about pursuing their core principles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, in fact running games where to wyld is the &quot;Big Bad&quot; and the garou are forced to work with weaver or wyrm aligned allies to hold the masquerade have been some of the best runs I've had. Especially in gehenna scenarios as having the world plunged into absolute chaos and the destruction of the masquerade seems like situations the wyld would simply love(likely with the help of tradition mages or changelings who'd love not having to deal with consensual paradox/banality)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T09:58:20-08:00","id":824394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/822738-question-on-the-wyld?p=824366#post824366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Right, And I didn't mean to imply that it did. I just meant that technology hadn't been invented yet in the time before dinosaurs.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>They had Wonder Working. It was.. like building an Archid form, but with dreams of objects instead of their reptilian heritage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah, in fact running games where to wyld is the &quot;Big Bad&quot; and the garou are forced to work with weaver or wyrm aligned allies to hold the masquerade have been some of the best runs I've had. Especially in gehenna scenarios as having the world plunged into absolute chaos and the destruction of the masquerade seems like situations the wyld would simply love(likely with the help of tradition mages or changelings who'd love not having to deal with consensual paradox/banality) </div> </div> </div>Tradition mages want some kind of order. Life with the Wyld would wear on them horribly, since what is and what isn't Paradox-causing would change constantly. Even Changelings favor a particular milieu that has points of stability. Living where everything is like an unleashing would probably not sit too well with them. Take note of how the most far gone of the Ratkin do, and then you have someone who's dedicated to the Wyld.<br /> <br /> (I wouldn't call anything really aligned with the Weaver or Wyrm an ally, even of convenience. They'd just be a different wall that the Garou and Fera were forcing their enemies toward. Rage makes dealing with figures like that even more temporary and acrimonious than the situation would suggest.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T16:07:11-08:00","id":824646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/822738-question-on-the-wyld?p=824394#post824394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tradition mages want some kind of order. Life with the Wyld would wear on them horribly, since what is and what isn't Paradox-causing would change constantly. Even Changelings favor a particular milieu that has points of stability. Living where everything is like an unleashing would probably not sit too well with them. Take note of how the most far gone of the Ratkin do, and then you have someone who's dedicated to the Wyld.<br /> <br /> (I wouldn't call anything really aligned with the Weaver or Wyrm an ally, even of convenience. They'd just be a different wall that the Garou and Fera were forcing their enemies toward. Rage makes dealing with figures like that even more temporary and acrimonious than the situation would suggest.)</div> </div> </div> </div>The mages/changeling don't need to KNOW that they're aiding the wyld.(this is why I love cwod, no one knows exactly whats going on)<br /> <br /> In one of said runs we interpreted the red star as the wyld gaining enough power to physically manifest in the real world by feeding off the rush of chaos during gehenna, but nobody knew that except the oldest and wisest fera and mages. Everyone else just understood it was a big glowing thing in the sky and everything started developing chaotic resonance.<br /> <br /> So all the mages may know is that something big happened in say the vamp community(like the withering randomly reshuffling generation), and the fighting between neonates and elders has started breaking out to public view. Enterprising mages would then start showing off vampire-like magic in these area's to help spread the existence of vampires(and by extension magic) to weaken the consensual paradigm. Yet in doing so they also help the wyld without knowing it, as the more mages being able to use magic without paradox means more mages falling to hubris and generating chaos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}